terone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 41     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm red and yellow  fibroadipose tissue fragment with a localizing needle and accompanying specimen radiograph  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm poorly defined  firm mass  with a tan cut surface  A portion of the mass is frozen as FX 1  saved frozen on Cox 5  The remainder the mass is submitted in A through C  with the rest of the specimen in D  Resident  DARRYL E  PALMER TOY  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LEFT BREAST MASS  IN SITU AND INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Ajit J  Alles  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
