Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  08 AUG 95 ACCESSIONED ON  08 AUG 95 at 18 57 CLINICAL DATA  45 year old women with history of nipple retraction and calcifications on X ray  status post core biopsy that was positive for comedo ductal carcinoma in situ                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  AND AXILLARY CONTENTS   1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  SEVERAL MICROSCOPIC FOCI SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM PRESENT IN A SINGLE SLIDE  GG   POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE III III    SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  COMEDO TYPE WITH MICROCALCIFICATIONS  SPANNING AT LEAST REMOVED_DATE CM  AND WITH FOCAL PAGET S DISEASE OF THE NIPPLE   SEE NOTE  3  ALL  EIGHTEEN  LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  4  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH MULTIPLE MACROCYSTS  5  RADIAL SCAR  MICROSCOPIC  6  RECENT HEMORRHAGE  GRANULATION TISSUE  FOCAL CHRONIC INFLAMMATION AND FOAMY MACROPHAGES CONSISTENT WITH PRIOR BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  Unequivical lymphatic blood vascular invasion is not seen  All margins are free of ductal carcinoma in situ and invasive carcinoma  Skin margins are free of Paget s disease  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Multiple levels examined  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  16 AUG 95 at 16 20                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The in situ tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The in situ tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  The sections stained for hormone receptor proteins do not contain invasive carcinoma  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 AUG 95 at 15 17 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  is a modified radical mastectomy specimen  consisting of left breast REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm  and overlying 21 0cm skin ellipse  a 1 1cm nipple with retraction  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary tail  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm area of breast parenchyma which contains multiple  dilated ducts containing a yellow semi solid material  These dilated ducts are located beneath the nipple  extend 0 1cm from the nipple surface  0 2cm from the inferior margin  2 0cm from the superior resection margin  3 0cm from the deep resection margin  approximately 3 0cm from the medial margin and 14 0cm from the lateral margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma on cross section reveals firm  tan to gray  rubbery tissue  intermixed with adipose tissue  There is no gross evidence of invasive carcinoma  The axillary adipose tissue is dissected to reveal multiple  firm  well circumscribed  lymph nodes that range in size from 0 2cm to 1 0cm  A frozen section is performed and the frozen tissue is saved frozen  SECTION CODE  A  area of dilated ducts which extend to the closest deep margin  relative to the closest deep margin B  area of dilated ducts with paste like intraluminal material closest to superior margin C D  representative section of dilated ducts with paste like material E G  representative sections of firm rubbery breast parenchyma  H  nearest deep resection margin from firm breast tissue I  representative sections of breast parenchyma J  representative section of nipple K Q  axillary lymph nodes R  breast parenchyma  0 5cm beneath the nipple S  dilated ducts with luminal paste like material  representative sections T  lateral aspect of dilated ducts with luminal paste like material U  representative section of nipple V  inferior skin margin closest to nipple with dilated ducts  0 2cm from margin  closest to mipple  en face  W  superior skin margin  closest to nipple  en face  X  medial skin margin Y  lateral skin margin Z  dilated ducts with paste like material  medial most extension of this area AA GG  Additonal sections of breast from areas of microcalcifications  Gross Description by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT AXILLARY CONTENTS    report_end  , Pathologic_size.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  KEVIN S  HUGHES  M D  Resident  Rajni V Mandal  M D  Signed Out by  Melinda J Lerwill  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  Atypical ductal hyperplasia  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT LOWER UPPER OUTER QUADRANT AREA OF CLIP   EXCISION  1  SMALL FOCI OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU ARISING IN A BACKGROUND OF MULTIFOCAL ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA FLAT EPITHELIAL ATYPIA  SEE NOTE AND TABLE  1  2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  3  RADIAL SCARS  4  SMALL DUCT PAPILLOMAS  5  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  6  MULTIPLE LEVELS EXAMINED  NOTE  Dr  Frederick Koerner has reviewed the case and concurs with the diagnosis of ductal carcinoma in situ  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU TUMOR SIZE  Scattered small foci in 4 of 10 blocks  GRADE  1  CALCIFICATIONS  In the ductal carcinoma in situ  atypical changes  and benign changes  MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Positive at the superior margin and  0 1cm from the posterior margin  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested  BREAST  LEFT UPPER UPPER OUTER QUADRANT AREA OF CALCIFICATION   EXCISION  1  SMALL FOCI OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU WITH ASSOCIATED MUCOCELE LIKE LESION  FOCAL EARLY MUCINOUS CARCINOMA CANNOT BE EXCLUDED  SEE NOTE AND TABLE  2  2  EXTENSIVE ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA FLAT EPITHELIAL ATYPIA  3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  4  INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMA WITH USUAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  NOTE  Several clusters of atypical epithelial cells are present in stromal mucin  raising the possibility of early mucinous carcinoma  Although some of the mucin and some fragments of epithelium appear to be artifactually displaced  the foci in question do not have this appearance  The epithelial clusters of concern in block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  are no longer present on deeper sections stained for calponin and p63  Dr  Frederick Koerner has reviewed the case and concurs with the interpretation  Multiple levels examined  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  2 DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU TUMOR SIZE  Scattered small foci in 3 of 10 blocks  GRADE  1  CALCIFICATIONS  Associated with the carcinoma in situ  atypical changes  and benign changes  MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Present at the anterior margin and  0 1cm from the inferior margin  The mucocele like lesion is also present at the posterior margin and  0 1cm from the anterior and superior margins  and re excision of these margins is suggested as well  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on the  lower upper outer quadrant  specimen  the carcinoma has a similar morphology in both specimens   By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are two containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh  labeled  lower upper outer quadrant area of clip   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm piece of yellow fibrofatty tissue  with stitches designating the anterior  lateral  and cephalad  superior  aspects of the specimen per the surgeon  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior   blue  posterior   black  superior   green and inferior   yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal multiple cysts ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 0 2cm  and surrounding firm parenchyma  A surgical clip is not grossly identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial margin  en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral margin  en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of remainder of specimen  submitted sequentially