Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  29 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  29 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 09 39 CLINICAL DATA  Large lump  left breast  positive mammogram  R O carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  MUCINOUS  COLLOID  CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor measures 1 2cm in greatest dimension and is focally present witin less then 0 1cm from inked margins  No definite vascular invasion is present  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Christophe Girardet  M D  Signed On  31 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 00                                                                                     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   1   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 372 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 3  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  10 MAY 93 at 11 10     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     RESULTS OF HORMONE BINDING ASSAYS AS REPORTED BY DAVID T  MACLAUGHLIN  PhD   726  REMOVED_CASE_ID   estrogen receptor  Positive 131 fm mg cytosolic protein  progesterone receptor  Not determined  insufficient tissue   Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 10 45 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned  revealing a well circumscribed  fleshy  tan nodule  REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 0 4cm  which abuts the inked margin  The remaining tissue is primarily unremarkable adipose tissue  A representative section of the nodule is frozen as Frozen Section  1 and the block is saved frozen  The remaining nodule is submitted entirely in A through C  The remaining tissue is submitted entirely in D through I  Resident  Metin Ozdemirli  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LEFT BTEAST  BX   MUCINOUS  COILOID  CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Jo Ann E  Haney  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  PART   LEFT BREAST   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  14 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  14 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13 15 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  1  MUCINOUS  COLLOID  CARCINOMA  INVASIVE  REMOVED_DATE CM  PRESENT AT SEVERAL INKED SURFACES   SEE NOTE  2  ATYPICAL INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  FOCAL ADJACENT TO INVASIVE CARCINOMA  NOTE  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  In the absence of an in situ component  a metastasis cannot be completely excluded  However  the cytomorphology of the tumor is most consistent with a breast primary  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 19 02                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 07 08 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm piece of firm  fibrofatty tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a white  firm nodule measuring 1 8cm in greatest dimension that focally abuts the inked margin  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  1  The specimen is submitted entirely in A through J  with frozen section in J  Resident  EDWIN S  MONUKI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT BREAST MASS  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Ross C  Wheeler  MD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
