Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  30 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  30 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 49 CLINICAL DATA  Excisional biopsy left breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE CARCINOMA  WITH DUCTAL AND LOBULAR FEATURES  REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE REMOVED_DATE OF 3  EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN ALONG A BROAD FRONT AND INVASIVE OF LYMPHATIC SPACES  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  SOLID AND CRIBRIFORM TYPE  ADJACENT TO THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  ABUTTING MARGINS  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 17 56                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 49     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Breast  Left   The tumor cells show strong overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  See note  Note  This test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 14 05 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  are five fragments of fibroadipose breast tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm in aggregate  The largest fragment measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm and is inked and sectioned to reveal multiple firm nodules ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 2 5cm in greatest dimension  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes A D  The second largest fragment measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm and is sectioned to reveal fibrofatty breast parenchyma  Representative sections of which are submitted in cassettes E H  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm nodular fragment is fibroadipose tissue with pink tan parenchyma is also present half of the specimen is submitted in cassette I  The remaining two fragments consists predominantly of unremarkable soft yellow fat and measure REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm in aggregate  Representative sections are submitted in cassette J  Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  