ssed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 52 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm mass of hard fibrofatty tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal a hard gritty irregular mass that replaces approximately 35  of the total area of the specimen and extends to several inked margins  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  1  and saved frozen  Representative sections of the remainder in A through J  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT    report_end  , Pathologic_size.
