ponding to the curvalinear scar  The biopsy cavity is surrounded by more firm  fibrous tissue with punctate areas of more yellow tissue  Approximately 0 5cm away from the biopsy cavity are more white  fibrous streaks  with more firm  focally gritty tissue  that comes to within 1 5cm of the closest inked deep margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma adjacent to and away from the biopsy cavity is composed of focally firm  nodular  fibrous tissue and grossly unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  Within the lateral breast tissue  no lymph nodes are grossly identified  SECTION CODE  A D  Representative sections of biopsy cavity in relation to closest overlying inked deep margin  E F  Representative sections of biopsy cavity in relation to overlying skin  including adjacent more firm areas of fibrous tissue surrounding biopsy cavity  G H  Representative sections of ill defined  firm nodules  each measuring approximately 0 3cm  adjacent to the biopsy cavity  Cassette H is in relation to closest inferior deep margin   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  stitch on highest axillary node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm piece of fibrofatty tissue  dissected to reveal no lymph nodes  Representative tissue is submitted in I and J  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1and2   LYMPH NODES  AXILLA   SMALL FOCUS OF METASTATIC CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  SELIM NASSER  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   RESECTION PART B  LYMPH NODES  HIGHEST AXILLARY NODE   EXCISION PART C  SENTINEL LYMPH NODE  AXILLA    report_end  , Pathologic.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  13 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  13 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 12 08 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  1  TUBULAR CARCINOMA  INVASIVE  0 5cm  FOCALLY EXTENDING TO AN INKED SURFACE  SEE NOTE   2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH MICROCYSTS  INTRALOBULAR FIBROSIS  AND APOCRINE METAPLASIA  3  MONCKEBERGS MEDIAL CALCIFIC SCLEROSIS  NOTE  Blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  carcinoma in situ is not present  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 51                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 AUG 95 at 12 53 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  in a container  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm fibrofatty fragment of breast tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm nodule  No frozen section done  The fragment is submitted entirely as follows  SECTION CODE  AandB  nodule CandD  regions flanking the nodule E M  unremarkable tissue  Enclosed is the lesions radiograph  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST  SUSPICIOUS NODULE  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  SAVED FOR PERMANENT SECTION  O R  Resident  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
