tive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 08 29 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in multiple parts  Received fresh from the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left lumpectomy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  There is a long suture designating the lateral margin and a short suture designating the superior margin  The specimen is inked in black and the superior lateral and posterior margin are overlayered with green  red and blue ink  respectively  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm stellate tan  white firm mass present at 0 3cm from the anterior margin  The surrounding breast tissue is white and firm and extends to the medial  superior and posterior margins  A representative section of the mass is frozen as FX 1 and resubmitted in cassette A  including the closest margin  The rest of the sections are submitted in cassettes B J  I and J are the lateral and medial margins submitted en face  Labeled  left additional deep breast tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm piece of fatty tissue  No mass is identified  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes K and L  Labeled  left axillary contents  and consists of a piece of fibrofatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm  Multiple lymph nodes are disected from this fatty tissue ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 2cm in greatest dimension  The lymph nodes are submitted in cassettes M Q  B and 