Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  20 REMOVED_MONTH 92 ACCESSIONED ON  20 REMOVED_MONTH 92 at 15 55 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast mass  history of ductal carcinoma in situ                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  1  TUBULAR CARCINOMA  80   FOCALLY PRESENT AT INKED SURGICAL MARGIN  AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  20   WITH CANCERIZATION OF LOBULES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  No definite vascular invasion is present  The invasive carcinoma is present in four slides and is 1 4cm in greatest dimension  Results of staining for estrogen and progesterone receptor will follow in an addendum  2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA AND APOCRINE METAPLASIA  3  MICROCALCIFICATIONS  Diagnosis by  Christophe Girardet  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 92 at 15 02                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the corresponding values were 97  and 95   respectively  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 breast carcinomas with determination of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy nine percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 97  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 92 at 14 56     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm fragment of soft  lobulated  yellow tissue with attached localizing wire and specimen x ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned  revealing a firm  tan area  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  extending to an inked margin  Entirely submitted for permanents in A through G  A   section nearest to needle   Gross Description by  John Allick Resident  Cynthia E  Flynn  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  HIGHLY SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE O R  Resident  Jane M  Yang  MD O R  Diagnosis by  John O Connell  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
