en cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 15 34 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  Left Breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with needle localization wires  oriented by the surgeon as to the superior and lateral aspects  The specimen is inked as follows  deep    black  anterior    blue  superior    yellow  and inferior    red  It is then sectioned to reveal no evidence of discrete mass lesions  but instead multiple areas where yellow  thick  caseous material can be expressed from ducts   0 1cm in diameter  These areas extend to within 0 2cm to 0 3cm of multiple inked margins  In the lateral aspect of the specimen  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm roundish  ill demarcated  firm area  0 3cm from the deep  and 0 8cm from the superior resection margins  This firm area is submitted entirely in Cassettes A C  All other margins are greater than 2 0cm away  Other areas are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE  D   Deep lateral  E   Deep and inferior  F   Superficial and superior  G   Deep  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left Axillary Contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fibrofatty tissue  The specimen is sectioned to reveal 10 lymph nodes  ranging in size from 0 3cm to 3 0cm in greatest diameter  The largest lymph node is bisected and submitted entirely in Cassettes H I  Another lymph node is bisected and submitted in Cassette J  two lymph nodes are submitted in Cassette K  and three lymph nodes are submitted in Cassettes L M  Gross Description by  JUSTIN M  CATES  MD Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD                      