ed to reveal unremarkable fibrofatty breast tissue which is entirely submitted as H  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast inferior margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm aggregate of tan pink unremarkable fibroadipose tissue with no orientation  The specimen is submitted in toto as I  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  superior medial posterior margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm portion of tan red fibroadipose tissue with no orientation  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal unremarkable tan yellow fibrofatty tissue  The specimen is entirely submitted as J L  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast anterior margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm aggregate of tan red unremarkable fibrofatty tissue with no orientation  The specimen is entirely submitted as M  Gross Description by  STEPHANIE KUEHN Resident  RANIA M  SELIEM  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY  SENTINEL   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN ONE LYMPH NODE  AWAIT KERATIN STAINS  O R  Resident  JULIA TURBINER  M D  O R  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL  EXCISION PART C  BREAST LEFT  LATERAL FINAL MARGIN  EXCISION PART D  BREAST LEFT  INFERIOR FINAL MARGIN  EXCISION PART E  BREAST LEFT  SUPERIOR MEDIAL MARGIN  EXCISION PART F  BREAST LEFT  ANTERIOR MARGIN  EXCISION , Pathologic_size.
