Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  09 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  09 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 57 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast ca                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  5 5 CM   METASTATIC TO THREE OF FIFTEEN AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  NOTE  The resection margin are free of carcinoma  Lymphatic vessel invasion is identified  BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  1  EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA WITH FOCAL ATYPIA  2  SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH FIBROSIS  CYST FORMATION AND APOCRINE METAPLASIA  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 14                                                                                     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   LEFT  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   5   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 372 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 3  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 26     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     RESULTS OF HORMONE BINDING ASSAYS AS REPORTED BY DAVID T  MACLAUGHLIN  PhD   726  REMOVED_CASE_ID   estrogen receptor  Positive 289 fm mg cytosolic protein progesterone receptor  Positive  REMOVED_CASE_ID  fm mg cytosolic protein Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 08 05 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  in two parts  Labeled  Right breast biopsy  is a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 1cm piece of rubbery  white tissue with admixed fat  The specimen is inked  sectioned and submitted in A and B  The next specimen consists of a left radical mastectomy specimen measuring 20 x 22 x 5cm with an attached 15 x 8 x 3cm axillary tail  The overlying skin measures 15 x 9cm and contains a slightly off center 3 5cm areola with a 1 2cm nipple  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 8cm well circumscribed  tan and vaguely rubbery tumor with rare cysts measuring 2 to 3mm is present superior to the nipple with overlying thinned  however not ulcerated skin  The tumor is present underneath the areola but does not grossly involve the nipple  The tumor is present 1 5cm from the deep resection margin  which is the nearest resection margin  The tumor is present 6cm from the medial resection margin  8cm from the superior resection margin  10 5cm from the inferior resection margin  and 20cm from the lateral axillary resection margin  The remainder of the breast tissue is tan white and rubbery with multiple cyst present measuring from 1mm to 1cm  Several cysts contain turbid green mucoid tissue  A gross photograph is taken  The remainder of the breast tissue also shows focal areas of punctate cloudy yellow    necrotic  tissue  Section Code  C  medial resection margin  D  superior resection margin  E  inferior resection margin  F G  representative sections of tumor and deep resection margin  H  another section of deep resection margin  I  representative section of tumor with irregular 0 8cm tan red area  J  representative section of tumor  skin and adjacent nipple  K  representative section of tumor and skin  L O  representative sections of remainder of breast tissue  P T  axillary lymph nodes ranging in size from 4mm to 1 5cm  U  other section of breast with separate tan  slight gritty 0 4cm nodule  This nodule is present 1 5cm superior to the main tumor and 4cm from the nearest resection margin  superior resection margin   V  BRDU tissue Resident  Elizabeth Bailey  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART A  LEFT BREAST   AXILLA PART B  RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  23 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  24 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 10 13 CLINICAL DATA  Forty seven year old with incidentally found left breast nodule  Biopsy showed extensive ductal carcinoma in situ                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  AND ADDITIONAL AXILLARY CONTENTS  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INFILTRATING  40   AND INTRADUCTAL  60   CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE II III   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The examined inked resection margins are free of carcinoma  Lymphatic invasion is not seen  Carcinoma is present in five of six slides of breast  Nipple is unremarkable  Fourteen of fourteen axillary lymph nodes are free of tumor  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 54                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 29     ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION Addendum     The residual tumor size is greater than 2cm in overall extent  Because of the multifocal nature of the carcinoma  a more accurate size cannot be expressed  No gross lesion was present  Added by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 30 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in two containers  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  Labeled  left breast  is a 22 x 18 x 4 8cm left breast with an attached 7 x 6 x 1 5cm portion of axillary tissue  The contained skin with unremarkable nipple measures REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  with a 6cm in length well healed scar along the superior margin  Two sutures are in place  a long suture laterally and a short suture superiorly  The axillary tissue contains multiple firm and enlarged lymph nodes  tan red on cut section and measuring up to 2 1cm in length  The breast parenchyma contains multiple confluent areas of linear tan gray firm tissue streaks  the largest confluent area REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  This confluent area contains cystic spaces filled with soft  yellow tan material  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm area of more red colored fibrous tissue  located medially and just beneath the medial border of the skin scar  No discrete biopsy cavity is noted  No discrete nodules are noted  The area of red colored fibrous tissue extends to within 2 5cm of the nearest margin  which is deep  Received fresh in a container  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional axillary tissue  is a 2 5cm in diameter aggregate of fibroadipose tissue which contains two fragmented lymph nodes  tan pink in color and measuring from REMOVED_DATE to 1 0cm in length  Section Code A   lymph nodes   additional axillary   2 B E   axillary tail lymph nodes  main specimen F   nipple and skin scar G H   red colored fibrous tissue  possible previous biopsy site I J   fibrous tissue with cystic areas containing soft tan material K M   representative breast tissue Resident  Kathleen K  Hansen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Michael J Yaremchuk  M D  PART A  POSITIONAL AXILLARY TISSUE PART B  LEFT BREAST and AXILLARY CONTENTS   report_end  , Pathologic.
