he remaining tissue consists of fat and dense gray white  rubbery  focally nodular  fibrous tissue  The axillary tissue contains multiple lymph node candidates  ranging REMOVED_DATE to 1 6cm in greatest dimension  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Aforementioned lesion  submitted entirely  with closest anterior and posterior resection margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue medial to scar   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue lateral to scar   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Sections of unremarkable upper inner quadrant  medial to lateral   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Sections of unremarkable lower inner quadrant  medial to lateral   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Sections of lower outer quadrant  medial to lateral   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Sections of upper outer quadrant  medial to lateral   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   2 lymph node candidates  bivalved  1 inked blue    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   5 lymph node candidates  submitted entirely   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   5 lymph node candidates  submitted entirely   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   5 lymph node candidates  submitted entirely   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   3 lymph node candidates  submitted entirely  Labeled  right additional axillary contents   are multiple fragments of fibrofatty tissue  aggregating to the 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm yielding a single lymph node candidate  0 4cm in greatest dimension  Submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The remainder of the specimen is submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M D   Electronically signed on Wednesday REMOVED_MONTH 16   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 11 06 33AM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART A  Breast  Right   Modified Radical Mastectomy PART B  Lymph Nodes  Additional Right Axilla   Dissection  report_end  , Pathologic_size.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  18 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  18 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 11 46 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  LARGER SPECIMEN   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU HARBORING CALCIFICATIONS AND CONFINED TO THE MASS  SCLEROSING ADENOSIS WITH CALCIFICATIONS  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  SEE NOTE  BREAST  LEFT  SMALLER SPECIMEN   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invsion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 08 09                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 08 02 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  accompanied by a radiograph   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a 8 x 5 x 2cm portion of fibrofatty breast tissue with needle localizing wires in place  and a second REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 0 8cm portion of fibroadipose tissue  The large piece is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 0 5cm tan  ill defined firm mass with multiple foci of tan  gritty material  extending to inked margin  Representative sections of this area is frozen as FX  1  and saved frozen  The remaining tissue is tan white  rubbery with multiple cysts  The mass with surrounding breast tissue are submitted in A through F  Representatives of the remaining tissue are in G through J  The smaller piece consists of predominantly fatty tissue  representative section is submitted in K  Resident  HENRY DONG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  POSITIVE FOR CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Lawrence R  Zukerberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
