Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  13 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  13 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 17 59 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE SUPERIOR MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN IN SEVERAL FOCI  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE MASS AND TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN IN SEVERAL FOCI  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  BREAST  LEFT   ANTERIOR SUPERIOR MARGIN    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  LEFT   ADDITIONAL SHAVED MARGIN    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA  SENTINEL    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY ON 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  LYMPH NODES  LET AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 13 OF 13 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 07 08                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 13 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass  is a 6 x REMOVED_DATE x 3cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  indicated with a long stitch lateral  short stitch superior  The specimen is inked black  superior overinked yellow  posterior overinked blue  and sectioned to reveal a 1 5cm hard white mass  0 2cm from the superior anterior margin and 0 4cm from the posterior margin  Tumor is submitted entirely in cassettes A through E  Representative sample of uninvolved breast in F  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast additional anterior superior margin  are fragments of fibroadipose tissue measuring 3 x 2 x 0 9cm in aggregate  Inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable breast parenchyma  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassette H through J  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional shaved margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 1 5cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  Sectioned to reveal fibrofatty breast parenchyma  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes K through P  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary contents  is a 6 x 6 x 3 5cm piece of fatty tissue containing lymph nodes  Multiple lymph nodes were found  The bigger nodes are bisected and half of each are submitted  The smaller nodes are submitted entirely in cassettes Q through T  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient sname  unit number  and  left axillary sentinel node  are fragments of soft tissue containing lymph nodes measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm in aggregate  Submitted entirely in cassette U  Resident  ZUOQIN TANG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST MASS   GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS FOR CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  HENRY DONG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  AMBULATORY GEN SURG   ACC 457 REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST LEFT  ANTERIOR SUPERIOR MARGIN   EXCISIONAL PART C  BREAST  LEFT   ADDITIONAL SHAVED MARGIN    EXCISIO PART D  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA  PART E  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION   report_end  , Pathologic_size.
